## Checks

Red (before the asset existed), exit 1:

```
{"asset":"lily-pad","ok":false,"forgeAll":{"exitCode":1,...},"failures":["forge all exited 1","missing out/lily-pad/lily-pad.glb",...]}
```

Look pass (check a), one call, `./forge render lily-pad --fast && ./forge inspect lily-pad --fast`:
the first profile (7.5 mm cells, 12 mm top samples) showed a wavy top surface and a soft rim roll.
Fix 1 sampled the dish and the curl every 3 mm, used a smoothstep curl that tops out at 0.032 m,
and set detail 0.0045. inspect then reported no warnings and no buried or floating part.
Fix 2 was the required `sdf.intersect` arity (the type check failed; the notch now nests two
binary intersects). I did not change the design in fix 2.

Green gate, `mech-check lily-pad`, exit 0:

```
{"asset":"lily-pad","ok":true,"forgeAll":{"exitCode":0,"warnings":[]},"triangles":3812,"bottomY":0,"files":{"glb":true,"stats":true,"render":true,"sprites":true,"glbBytes":788960},"typecheckExit":0,"failures":[]}
```

Check b, one call: mech-check ok, then `./forge cutout ... --views front,three-quarter`, then
`node scripts/cutout-check.mjs out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props` (last line "result ok"), then
`python3 scripts/review-cards.py out/prop-cards lily-pad` (wrote out/prop-cards/lily-pad.png).
