## Known weak points

- The front cutout of a flat ground prop is a 34 px sliver (rows 974..1008 of 1024) because the
  cutout camera frames the model's height. The veins do not show in the cutout. The forge
  turnaround and the 8-direction sprite sheet do show them. The scene needs a top-down or a high
  three-quarter camera to see the vein fan.
- The frog's feet (0.347 m x 0.222 m) leave about 26 mm of leaf at the widest point and reach the
  notch edge. The brief fixes the 0.40 m width, so I did not change it. No frog-on-pad render
  exists yet.
- The vein colour #4f8f5a on #5fa364 is a low contrast pair. At the 128 px sprite size the veins
  read as faint lines; in the 1024 cutout they read.
- The V notch edges are sharp (a cut, not a bevel). The mesh cells are 4.5 mm, so the notch edge
  steps by about one cell.
- The rim curl adds 12 mm over the outer 30 mm. In the front view it reads as a thickened end, not
  as a tall lip, because the pad is only 20 mm thick.
- Width, thickness, notch angle, greens, and vein count are PM defaults: the book gives no size and
  no colour. The brief marks each one "PM default, check against the book".
- I did not rate my own work.

